# Phase C — declarative apt source for Microsoft Visual Studio Code.
#
# OPT-IN — the matching apps.toml entry ships `enabled = false`.  The
# dotfiles default is VSCodium (open-source rebuild without MS telemetry).
# Microsoft VSCode is included here because the user's actual workflow
# uses Microsoft-marketplace-only extensions (Python tooling, Jupyter,
# Remote-SSH, GitHub Copilot Chat) that Open VSX cannot ship.
#
# Telemetry posture: the dotfiles-shipped settings.json sets
# `telemetry.telemetryLevel = "off"` + a half-dozen related keys.
# Microsoft still receives the apt-fetch HTTP traffic itself; the
# binary just doesn't phone home after install.
#
# Signing-key fingerprint pinned in config/apps/apps.toml.  Source of
# truth (rotation cadence multi-year, Microsoft release signing key):
#   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/linux/install
#   https://packages.microsoft.com/keys/microsoft.asc

Types: deb
URIs: https://packages.microsoft.com/repos/code
Suites: stable
Components: main
Architectures: amd64 arm64
Signed-By: /etc/apt/keyrings/microsoft-keyring.asc
